            "<p>Indus Valley Civilisation</p>",
            "<p>Sites at Rakhigarhi (largest IVC site), Banawali, Mitathal, Bhirrana (oldest at ~7570 BC)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vedic Period</p>",
            "<p>Battle of Ten Kings (Dasharajna) fought on Ravi; Kurukshetra – birthplace of Bhagavad Gita</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mahabharata Period</p>",
            "<p>Kurukshetra war fought here; Panipat region part of ancient Kuru kingdom</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mauryan Empire</p>",
            "<p>Part of Ashokan empire; Buddhist influence at Topra (Ashokan pillar later moved to Delhi)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Post-Mauryan</p>",
            "<p>Ruled by Sungas, Kushanas, Guptas successively</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Medieval Period</p>",
            "<p>Three Battles of Panipat (1526, 1556, 1761) – decisive battles of Indian history</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
